  "candidate_0008": {
    "reason": "The claim that a causal attention mask restricts the attention matrix to be lower-triangular is factually incorrect. A causal mask enforces $Attention(i, j) = 0$ for $j > i$ (future tokens), which results in an upper-triangular structure (assuming standard row=source, col=target indexing). Lower-triangularity would imply blocking past tokens and allowing future ones, violating the autoregressive constraint. The objection correctly identifies this geometric error; therefore, the claim must be withdrawn.",
    "candidate_id": "candidate_0008",
    "position": "withdraw"
  }
}
